{{.Note}}

What an agent can do with media depends on the provider it runs on: an agent has exactly the modalities of its provider. This matrix is computed from the provider drivers shipped in AgentOven {{.Version}}, so it cannot drift from the code. For how to switch a modality on or off, see [Provider modalities](/modalities).

## Matrix

{{.Table}}

Yes means the driver and the sample model support it by default. No means it is not available without an override, or not at all.

## How to read it

- **Image, PDF and video** are decided per model, using the model catalog and the driver's defaults. The sample model shown is the one this matrix was computed with; another model of the same kind can differ. Set `config.modalities` on the provider to turn a modality on for a gateway whose models the catalog does not know, or off for one you do not want used.
- **PDF** is "yes" for any model that is not switched off: a model without native PDF input gets the extracted text instead.
- **Speech** means the driver has a speech-to-text and text-to-speech API. Cascaded voice calls use the agent's own provider only; voice never borrows another provider's speech.
- **Realtime** means the driver can open a live speech-to-speech session. Calling it from the control plane is an AgentOven Pro feature.
- **Web search** is the provider's own built-in search. It is the one modality that is off until you switch it on (`config.modalities.web.enabled: true`), and with Gemini it cannot be combined with function tools.

<Callout type="note">

Pro adds more provider drivers (for example cloud-hosted model services); they are not in this matrix, which covers the open-source drivers.

</Callout>

